<p>Explain why the molar enthalpies of vaporization of the following substances increase in the order CH<sub>4</sub> &lt; C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub> &lt; C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>8</sub>, even though all three substances experience the same dispersion forces when in the liquid state.</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/10.E:_Liquids_and_Solids_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_71"><span id="S10.3.16"></span><h3 id="S10.3.16-42535">S10.3.16 </h3>

