<p>Thallium(I) iodide crystallizes with the same structure as CsCl. The edge length of the unit cell of TlI is 4.20 &Aring;. Calculate the ionic radius of TI<sup>+</sup>. (The ionic radius of I<sup>&minus;</sup> is 2.16 &Aring;.)</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/10.E:_Liquids_and_Solids_(Exercises)" class="mt-section"><span id="S10.6.25"></span><h3 id="S10.6.25-42535">S10.6.25 </h3>

